# THE REAPER BY FORCE, ITS LAST PHASE, PLAYED WITH THE KEYS (roadmap slice 1,
# step 4). Stooped, it grips instead of biting and hauls the player off, and it
# turns on the spot as fast as a player can circle it, on a shore fenced either
# side; the chute gear at its back is the one open part left. Pulled loose (the
# swing key, twice with the steel knife) the wrench slews the gantry half round
# and jams it (Blow.torn): its gear glows toward the player, who steps in and
# takes it. Again, until it falls. Brought to that phase by `wound`; everything
# after is the real walk, run and swing. The whole fight from full health is
# tests/sentinel/test_reaper_force.gd.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/reaper_torn.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --held=knife_shear --config=unharmed
coast calm
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
near keeper
await sentinel 12
wait 3.0
wound sentinel.coast 0.25
wait 0.3
try 4
  walkto mob 6
  await grip 8
end
shot 01-stooped-it-grips-and-hauls with shoulder,mob:sentinel.coast,grip
tap swing
wait 0.2
tap swing
await free 1
walkto part 2 run
tap swing
await hit 0.8
shot 02-torn-loose-it-slews-and-jams-the-gear-taken with shoulder,torn
try 8
  walkto mob 4
  await grip 6
  tap swing
  wait 0.2
  tap swing
  await free 1
  walkto part 2 run
  tap swing
  wait 0.6
  tap swing
  wait 0.6
  tap swing
  await sentinel_dead 0.6
end
wait 1.5
shot 04-it-falls-to-the-keys with shoulder,sentinel_dead
